  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 229 AM EDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nThe drier conditions we are currently enjoying will be short lived \nas a upper level trough digs across eastern CONUS pushing a \nassociated boundary to the southeast across our area. This set up \nwith drive a southwest flow and provide ample cloud cover with \nwidespread showers and thunderstorms by the start of the weekend. \nOne benefit of the wetter conditions is a reduction in the afternoon \nhigh temperatures by several degrees through the first of next week. \nThe wetter pattern will continue through the tuesday with with PWATS \nrange from the 2-2.5\" range through Sunday. While we are not \ncurrently expecting to reach severe criteria at this time, \nhowever, the widespread convection will allow for a few strong \nstorms with gusty winds, and localized flash flooding conditions. \n\nModels continue to show variability beyond mid week on how \nquickly the upper low shifts away from the forecast area. There \nare indications some drier air will work into the CWA by mid week,\nbut more time is required for the pattern to resolve. At this \ntime, continue to advertise PoPs trending more scattered by \nmidweek as a result of aforementioned variability.",
